CloudBurrow patch 53 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1522). Applies after patch 0045.

routines.insert made the function in the engine's catalog alone, and
routines.get and routines.list, which read the emulator's metadata store,
were stubs ("unsupported bigquery.routines.get", 500). So CloudBurrow's
front, which serves those methods from what it sees made, knew nothing of
a function routines.insert made before it started, and a deletion of its
dataset could not keep it for undelete. The patch keeps each Routine
routines.insert makes in the metadata store (replacing one of the same
ID), with creation and modification times by the engine's clock, and
routines.get and routines.list answer what it keeps.

